WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.440
Want to try the version one laptop prototype?

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.720
Clone the repo on your laptop.

3
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.190
Connect your mic to an XLR-to-USB audio interface,

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.620
and the interface output to the console.

5
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.450
Install the package.

6
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.780
List your devices, pick the input and the output,

7
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.820
then run it in real time.

8
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:25.400
You'll need a 64-bit laptop
running Python 3.10 or newer,

9
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:31.100
and an interface with at least one XLR mic input
and a line-level output.

10
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:37.310
For the closed loop, just feed a line-level copy
of the speaker feed into a second input.

11
00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:43.850
Start at 48 kHz, with a 128 to 256 sample callback.

12
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:49.820
Watch the times that nullyn rt prints,
and raise the block size if you need to.

13
00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:53.330
It's open source, and it's in active development.

14
00:00:53.684 --> 00:00:55.014
nullyn.ai
